{
	"_comment": "Automatic update-check schedule vectors. The canonical JavaScript (_shared/modules/updater/schedule.js), the shared Lua port (_shared/lua/updater/schedule.lua, macOS and Linux) and the AHK port (windows/modules/updater/schedule.ahk) replay this file with the timing of defaults.json, so the three drivers cannot disagree on when a check is due. Times are wall-clock epoch seconds. started_at is when the driver started or the system last woke. A state field that is absent is omitted (the shared Lua decoder turns a JSON null into a non-nil sentinel), and an expected result without due_at means no check is ever due. The jitter expectations were computed outside the three ports: h = fold of (h * 31 + byte) mod 2147483647 over the UTF-8 bytes of '<seed>:<anchor>', span = min(floor(interval * jitter_percent / 100), jitter_max_sec), jitter = h mod (span + 1).",
	"due": [
		{
			"id": "fresh_install_waits_for_the_boot_delay",
			"now": 1700000000,
			"started_at": 1700000000,
			"interval": 86400,
			"state": { "seed": "7f3a9c21e5b04d68" },
			"expect": { "reason": "first_check", "due_at": 1700000030 }
		},
		{
			"id": "fresh_install_evaluated_after_the_boot_delay",
			"now": 1700000100,
			"started_at": 1700000000,
			"interval": 86400,
